    "description": "SheTrades Sri Lanka launches export guides in local languages to help women-led SMEs access UK market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/SheTrades-Sri-Lanka-launches-export-guides-in-local-languages-to-help-women-led-SMEs-access-UK-market/273-345750",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1784175089.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-07-16-dailymirrorlk-98d7c279-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "17a11e224ac94128798e86585572ab03",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1694,
    "chunk_text": "SheTrades Sri Lanka launches export guides in local languages to help women-led SMEs access UK market\n\nThe SheTrades Sri Lanka Hub has launched sector-specific export handbooks in Sinhala and Tamil, aimed at helping the women entrepreneurs and small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) improve their readiness to export to the UK, leveraging preferential market access available under the UK\u2019s Developing Countries Trading Scheme (DCTS).\n\nThe handbooks, developed by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), in collaboration with the International Trade Centre and British High Commission in Colombo, focus on the textiles and apparel sector, including women\u2019s accessories, footwear and handicrafts as well as processed agrifood and spices.\n\nThe guides provide practical information on export procedures, regulatory requirements and market expectations in the UK, while also outlining the opportunities under the DCTS, which grants duty-free access to around 92 percent of product lines exported from Sri Lanka to the UK.\n\nThe initiative is part of the UK government-funded SheTrades Commonwealth+ Programme, which seeks to strengthen the competitiveness and international market access of women-led export-oriented businesses across the Commonwealth countries.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe said the UK remained an important trading partner for Sri Lanka and highlighted the opportunities available through the DCTS framework.\n\n\u201cThe UK\u2019s DCTS presents a golden opportunity for Sri Lankan enterprises to enter and scale within the UK market, under the preferential access arrangements,\u201d Abeysinghe said."
  },
