    "chunk_text": "Speaking at the launch, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe said the UK remained an important trading partner for Sri Lanka and highlighted the opportunities available through the DCTS framework.\n\n\u201cThe UK\u2019s DCTS presents a golden opportunity for Sri Lankan enterprises to enter and scale within the UK market, under the preferential access arrangements,\u201d Abeysinghe said.\n\nLord Hannett said translating the handbooks into Sinhala and Tamil would make export-related information more accessible to the entrepreneurs across the country, helping a wider group of businesses better understand the UK market requirements and opportunities.\n\nThe EDB said the handbooks are intended to improve export readiness among the women entrepreneurs and SMEs while supporting broader efforts to promote inclusive, export-led growth in Sri Lanka."
