    "md5": "0bceb6288ffecf52a4b1f8aa173b6a6a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1705,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Cabral, a leading corporate and commercial lawyer and a Chambers Asia-Pacific Band 1 ranked practitioner for Dispute Resolution, will deliver a keynote address titled \u201cBeyond Compliance: How Boards Create Sustainable Value for All Stakeholders.\u201d Drawing on his extensive experience in law, regulation, and board leadership, he will examine how directors can move beyond traditional compliance obligations to become catalysts for long-term value creation.\n\nThe program will also feature SEC Chairman Senior Professor Hareendra Dissabandara, whose extensive experience spanning academia, capital markets, regulation, and public policy will provide valuable perspectives during the panel discussion \u201cEffective Boards Don\u2019t Just Comply \u2013 They Lead.\u201d\n\nAdding an international diplomatic dimension to the Summit, Ambassador of the Republic of T\u00fcrkiye to Sri Lanka Semih L\u00fctf\u00fc Turgut will participate in the prestigious Directors\u2019 Dialogue, sharing perspectives on global cooperation, leadership, and the importance of strong governance in an increasingly interconnected world.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026 aims to strengthen investor confidence, promote governance excellence, and support Sri Lanka\u2019s ambition to develop a more competitive, resilient, and sustainable corporate sector.\n\nBy bringing together eminent leaders from business, banking, law, regulation, academia, diplomacy, and international finance, the Summit will provide a unique platform for directors, CEOs, senior executives, policymakers, and governance professionals to engage with emerging trends, address boardroom challenges, and collectively shape the future of corporate leadership in Sri Lanka."
  },
