    "chunk_size_bytes": 1336,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018HyperCon 2026\u2019 set to storm Colombo this August\n\nHyperCon 2026, poised to be one of the island\u2019s largest gaming, esports, and digital entertainment conventions, will officially take over the capital this August.\n\nOrganized by NXL Entertainment in collaboration with TRIOSLK, the massive two-day convention is scheduled for the 1st and 2nd of August.\u00a0 The event will turn the Royal MAS Arena and the Royal College Union (RCU) Skills Centre in Colombo 07 into a high-octane hub for the country\u2019s digital generation.\n\nHyperCon 2026 isn\u2019t just an esports tournament; it is a holistic celebration of modern pop culture. The convention aims to unite esports athletes, casual gamers, cosplayers, content creators, and fans from every corner of Sri Lanka under one roof. The event is projected to attract over 4,000 on-site visitors and reach an explosive digital audience of more than 100,000 people through high-quality professional livestreams, match highlights, creator collaborations, and extensive online coverage.\n\nAt the heart of HyperCon 2026 are the highly anticipated Esports Championships. Gamers will battle it out across major titles including PUBG Mobile, Mobile Legends: Bang Bang (MLBB), Free Fire, and e-Chess, featuring competitive prize pools and professional tournament management complete with live commentary."
