    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3aca4cd41cd8f22d1db42189900b2700",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "Global banking, governance, regulatory to headline Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026\n\nSri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026, organised by the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID), will be held on July 22, 2026, at Cinnamon Grand Colombo, under the theme \u2018Future-Ready Sri Lankan Directors: From Compliance to Sustainable Growth\u2019.\n\nThe summit will bring together an exceptional gathering of global banking leaders, governance experts, regulators, legal authorities, diplomats and corporate directors to exchange insights, share international best practices and explore the evolving role of boards in building resilient, innovative and sustainable organisations.\n\nThe summit will feature an outstanding line-up of distinguished speakers, including HSBC Holdings PLC Independent Non-Executive Director Kalpana Morparia. She is former Chairman of J.P. Morgan South and Southeast Asia and recipient of India\u2019s prestigious Padma Shri Award (2024).\u00a0 Morparia will deliver a keynote address on \u2018The Changing Role of Bank Directors: From Fiduciary Oversight to Strategic Stewardship\u2019, sharing perspectives from her distinguished career in global banking and board leadership.\n\nJoining her will be two of Sri Lanka\u2019s most respected corporate governance and legal experts\u2014National Savings Bank and Tokyo Cement Company (Lanka) PLC Chairman Dr. Harsha Cabral, PC and CIC Holdings PLC and Sampath Bank PLC Chairman Harsha Amarasekera, PC.\n\nDr. Cabral, a leading corporate and commercial lawyer and a Chambers Asia-Pacific Band 1-ranked practitioner for dispute resolution, will deliver a keynote address titled \u2018Beyond Compliance: How Boards Create Sustainable Value for All Stakeholders\u2019.\n\nDrawing on his extensive experience in law, regulation and board leadership, he will examine how the directors can move beyond traditional compliance obligations to become catalysts for long-term value creation."
  },
