    "chunk_size_bytes": 1489,
    "chunk_text": "Drawing on his extensive experience in law, regulation and board leadership, he will examine how the directors can move beyond traditional compliance obligations to become catalysts for long-term value creation.\n\nThe programme will also feature Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Chairman Senior Prof. Hareendra Dissabandara, whose extensive experience spanning academia, capital markets, regulation and public policy will provide valuable perspectives during the panel discussion \u2018Effective Boards Don\u2019t Just Comply \u2013 They Lead\u2019.\n\nAdding an international diplomatic dimension to the summit, Ambassador of the Republic of T\u00fcrkiye to Sri Lanka Semih L\u00fctf\u00fc Turgut will participate in the prestigious Directors\u2019 Dialogue, sharing perspectives on global cooperation, leadership and the importance of strong governance in an increasingly interconnected world.\n\nSri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026 aims to strengthen investor confidence, promote governance excellence and support Sri Lanka\u2019s ambition to develop a more competitive, resilient and sustainable corporate sector.\n\nBy bringing together eminent leaders from business, banking, law, regulation, academia, diplomacy and international finance, the summit will provide a unique platform for directors, CEOs, senior executives, policymakers and governance professionals to engage with the emerging trends, address boardroom challenges and collectively shape the future of corporate leadership in Sri Lanka."
