    "md5": "835f0655b16f6f35ea24f105b910c3c7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1731,
    "chunk_text": "Vietnam envoy dubs SL a \u2018hidden gem in the Indian Ocean\u2019\n\nDescribing Sri Lanka as a \u201chidden gem in the Indian Ocean,\u201d Vietnam\u2019s Ambassador to Sri Lanka Trinh Thi Tam highlighted the massive untapped potential awaiting discovery as the two nations prepare to enter a new era of direct air connectivity.\n\nSpeaking at a high-level seminar titled \u2018Amazing Vietnam is Calling, Let\u2019s Vietjet\u2019 in Colombo last week, the Ambassador emphasised that the true beauty and economic synergy of both nations remained obscured by logistical barriers\u2014a reality set to change dramatically on August 18.\n\n\u201cAir connectivity has always been one of the most important drivers for tourism growth,\u201d the Ambassador stated. \u201cToday, traveling between Vietnam and Sri Lanka often requires long transit times through third countries including Thailand, Malaysia, and Singapore. Even the embassy staff, whenever we want to travel back to Vietnam, it takes us a lot of time.\u201d\n\nThe upcoming launch of direct flights between Ho Chi Minh City and Colombo by Vietjet Air is expected to serve as a critical milestone. The new scheduled service will operate three round-trip flights per week on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays. \u201cWith the new Vietjet service, I think that it will help us to significantly shorten travel time, make the journeys more convenient and affordable, and encourage more people to discover each other\u2019s beautiful countries,\u201d she added.\n\nThe Ambassador noted that this development will also help to bring both nations closer together, facilitate business exchanges, strengthen tourism cooperation, and deepen the friendship that Vietnam and Sri Lanka have built over more than 55 years of diplomatic relations."
