    "md5": "75faf07a76936e8c77c2da1589a37d15",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka, BASL partner to strengthen professional collaboration via strategic MoU\n\nThe MoU was signed by CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe (right) and BASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya, marking an important step in enhancing cooperation between two of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading professional bodies\n\nThe Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka) and the Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on 17 July to strengthen engagement between the accounting and legal professions, promoting knowledge exchange, professional development, and other initiatives of mutual interest.\n\nThe partnership seeks to provide a platform for both professions to engage on matters of common interest, recognising the increasingly interconnected nature of legal, financial, and regulatory matters in today\u2019s business environment.\n\nUnder the MoU, CA Sri Lanka and the BASL will explore opportunities for joint initiatives, including continuing professional development programs, knowledge-sharing forums, technical discussions, and other capacity-building activities aimed at enhancing the competencies of members of both professions.\n\nCA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe highlighted the importance of closer collaboration between the accounting and legal professions.\n\n\u201cAs the business environment continues to evolve, there is significant value in our professions working together to support organisations, strengthen governance, and contribute to the country\u2019s development,\u201d he said.\n\nHe further noted that the MoU reflects CA Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to fostering professional engagement, facilitating the exchange of knowledge, and creating learning opportunities that benefit members and the wider professional community.\n\nBASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya described the MoU as a significant milestone in the relationship between the two professions."
  },
