    "chunk_text": "Representing three of Sri Lanka\u2019s top corporate leaders, they will reflect on leading organisations through periods of disruption, driving transformation and making strategic decisions that create enduring value. Muhseen brings more than 25 years of regional and international investment banking experience, having held senior leadership positions at JPMorgan, Merrill Lynch and Credit Suisse, he was the Joint Awardee of the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors \u2018Most Outstanding Independent Director Award in 2025. Together, the three leaders will offer delegates candid perspectives on leadership, resilience, governance and the boardroom decisions that shape successful organisations.\n\nMore than a conference, the Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026 is a platform for directors, CEOs and senior executives to exchange ideas, challenge conventional thinking and learn from globally respected leaders who are shaping the future of governance. Participants will gain practical insights into emerging boardroom priorities, evolving governance expectations and the leadership capabilities required to succeed in a rapidly changing business environment.\n\nBy fostering stronger governance, promoting responsible leadership and encouraging boardroom excellence, the Summit seeks to strengthen investor confidence and support Sri Lanka\u2019s ambition to build a more competitive, resilient and sustainable corporate sector. As boards confront an increasingly dynamic global landscape, the Summit offers a timely opportunity to learn from leaders at the forefront of corporate transformation, governance excellence and sustainable value creation."
