    "chunk_text": "The 2026 World cup tournament had a number of other shortcomings as well. Players and teams continue publicly protesting refereeing decisions. A senior member of the coaching staff of a particular country ran on to the playing field to challenge a particular decision and had to be ordered off the field.\n\nIt would appear that players, politicians and even members of the coaching staff (who should be maintaining standards) are beginning to feel that they are bigger than the game itself. It is time FIFA tightened rules governing the actions of its administrators of the game. Else, soon the game will actually descend to the level of ruffians, who\u00a0 Sadly happen to be\u00a0 idols of the young\u00a0 the world over.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
