    "md5": "d9a0095f0121c221963f2db9fc740b62",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "China\u2019s global popularity rises as US stumbles\n\nTrump\u2019s off-the-cuff threats, the weaponisation of tariffs and the indecisive Iran campaign have together dented his global image and that of the US, while that of President Xi Jinping and China has brightened\n\nThis year, China\u2019s global popularity has risen while that of the US has stumbled, says the latest Pew Research Centre survey. The survey was based on a population of 42,151 adults in 36 countries across the globe. It was conducted between February 8 and May 13 this year.\n\nUS President Donald Trump\u2019s off-the-cuff threats, the weaponisation of tariffs and the indecisive Iran campaign have together dented his image and that of the US, vis-\u00e0-vis President Xi Jinping and China.\n\nInterestingly, the US is viewed more positively than China in just six of the 36 countries -- India, Japan, the Philippines and South Korea.\n\nIn 2025, global views of the United States had worsened as President Donald Trump\u2019s second term began, though most people still had a more positive opinion of the US than of China. But this year, that is no longer the case. For the first time in Pew surveys, China is ahead of the US. Views of China have turned more positive \u2013 and views of the US more negative \u2013 across 20 of the 36 countries.\n\nDuring the first two years of President Trump\u2019s second term, his ratings worsened significantly. While many people still lack confidence in Xi, positive views of the Chinese President have become more widespread.\u00a0 More now say that they have confidence in Xi than in Trump.\n\nOne area where the US still gets higher ratings than China is \u201cpersonal freedoms.\u201d More say that the US government respects the personal freedoms of its people. Still, the gap has been narrowing \u2013 driven by \u201clarge drops\u201d in the shares saying the US government respects personal freedoms."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
