    "chunk_size_bytes": 1034,
    "chunk_text": "It was further submitted that the unauthorised alteration and exploitation of the film constituted an infringement of the plaintiff\u2019s moral rights, copyright and related rights under the Intellectual Property Act.\n\nChandran Rutnam\u2019s film, 'Rizana: A Caged Bird' was inspired by the tragic story of Rizana Nafeek, a young Sri Lankan domestic worker from the Eastern Province of Sri Lanka, who was recruited and sent to the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia to work as a domestic worker on a forged passport as a minor who was subsequently executed.\n\nChandran Rutnam being deeply moved by the gravity and significance of this story, considered it his moral and creative obligation as a filmmaker to bring this story to the world stage, given its profound implications for the exploitation of Sri Lankan workers abroad and the vulnerability of young women in foreign employment.\n\nUpul Jayasiruya PC, together with Laknath Senavirathna, Naduni Madara and Yashodha Fernando instructed by Invictus Law appeared for the plaintiff, Chandran Rutnam."
