    "md5": "604be12004e3ef71a2fccb4a533587cb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1604,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s first youth business program launches in Colombo, as Teen Academy opens its inaugural cohort on 8 August\n\nTeen Master of Business brings a Wharton and Harvard-benchmarked entrepreneurship curriculum to Sri Lankan teenagers, complementing their schooling with hands-on, real-world business experience\n\nTeen Academy, a new business education program for secondary school students, will open its first cohort in Colombo on 8 August, offering Sri Lankan teenagers a structured introduction to entrepreneurship alongside their regular schooling.\n\nThe program, called the Teen Master of Business, is built around twelve live modules, real micro-enterprise launches, and accredits business competencies, and is benchmarked against international youth business programs including Wharton Global Youth and Clever Harvey\u2019s Junior MBA. The inaugural cohort will run from August 2026 to January 2027 at the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM) in Colombo.\n\nTeen Academy is founded and run by Bradley Emerson\u00a0 under Business Athletes Ltd., a Sri Lanka-based reputed corporate training, executive coaching, and strategic consulting firm.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka has every ingredient other markets have built on \u2014 high literacy, English-medium capability, a young population, and no shortage of ambition,\u201d said Teen Academy and Business Athletes Ltd. Founder Bradley Emerson. \u201cOur schools already give students a strong academic foundation. What Teen Academy adds is the capability to apply it \u2014 to build something real, pitch it, and learn what it takes to lead, well before they turn eighteen.\u201d"
  },
