    "md5": "eb12e4cfa6fd7d85bc7d2b3f3a2a64a4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "Wildlife holiday bungalows to be upgraded\n\nColombo, July 22 (Daily Mirror) - The government has planned to upgrade holiday bungalows managed by the Departments of Wildlife Conservation and Forest Conservation, using modern technology to provide improved facilities for the public.\n\nThe matter was discussed during a meeting held this afternoon at the Presidential Secretariat under the patronage of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to review the progress of projects implemented under the 2026 budget allocations for the Ministry of Environment and to discuss proposals for the 2027 Budget.\n\nThe President instructed officials to take the maximum possible measures to protect the rapidly developing Northern and Eastern coastlines.\n\nThe President also directed that the strongest possible legal action be taken to prevent unauthorised constructions after coastal development, noting that such activities cause significant damage to the coastline.\n\nThe President further instructed that a steering committee be appointed to oversee and monitor these efforts.\n\nThe meeting also extensively reviewed the progress of projects implemented by the Ministry of Environment under the theme \u201cA Thriving Nation - A Beautiful Life, A Sustainable Biosphere \u2013 A Green Life\", with a total budget allocation of Rs. 19,719 million, as well as the Ministry's plans for 2027, the President's Media Division (PMD) said.\n\nThe meeting reviewed the progress of recurrent and capital expenditure incurred in 2026 by institutions under the Ministry of Environment, including the Central Environmental Authority, Department of Wildlife Conservation, Forest Department, Department of National Zoological Gardens, Department of National Botanic Gardens, the Water Resources Board, Department of Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management and the Marine Environment Protection Authority."
  },
