    "chunk_size_bytes": 1395,
    "chunk_text": "The meeting reviewed the progress of recurrent and capital expenditure incurred in 2026 by institutions under the Ministry of Environment, including the Central Environmental Authority, Department of Wildlife Conservation, Forest Department, Department of National Zoological Gardens, Department of National Botanic Gardens, the Water Resources Board, Department of Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management and the Marine Environment Protection Authority.\n\nThe President paid particular attention to the progress of projects implemented under the 2026 Budget to mitigate the human-elephant conflict in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe President pointed out that the slow implementation of these projects poses a direct threat to human lives and stressed that delays are unacceptable when the necessary budgetary provisions have already been allocated.\n\nEmphasising the need to be sensitive to the lives and livelihoods of the rural communities, President Dissanayake instructed officials to complete these projects within the stipulated time frame and to fully utilise the budget allocations made for this year by carrying out the relevant construction and implementation activities before the end of the year.\n\nThe President further emphasised that the location and extent of elephant fences should be determined based on the need to protect human lives rather than merely to demarcate wildlife zones."
