    "md5": "ae20cfcdd9f9b7e9403988dfca446c30",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1770,
    "chunk_text": "China ready to work with Sri Lanka to build strategic trust: Chinese Ambassador\n\nColombo, July 22 (Daily Mirror) - Military cooperation between China and Sri Lanka has been further deepened in multiple fields in recent years, covering defense consultations, personnel training, equipment and technical exchanges, Chinese Ambassador to Sri Lanka Qi Zhenhong said.\n\nAddressing an event to mark the 99th anniversary of the founding of the People\u2019s Liberation Army (PLA), he said the military-to-military relations between China and Sri Lanka are battle-tested.\n\n\u201cIn the aftermath of Cyclone Ditwah, China provided the Sri Lankan Ministry of Defence with supplies valued at 10 million RMB. As always, China stands ready to work with Sri Lanka to build strategic trust and continue to firmly support each other,\u201d he said.\n\nOn the occasion of the 99th anniversary of the founding of the Chinese People's Liberation Army(PLA), on behalf of the Chinese Embassy in Sri Lanka, I would like to pay my highest respects to the glorious PLA and express my heartfelt gratitude to all friends who have cared for and supported China's national defense and military modernization!\n\nThis year marks the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, as well as the 90th anniversary of the victory of the Long March, and the opening year of the 15th Five-Year Plan. Looking back on China's remarkable achievements, the most fundamental guarantee is the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China. Entering the new era, under the guidance of President Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military,\u00a0 the PLA upgrades military equipment, optimizes troop structure and enhances overall combat capabilities to safeguard national security and global peace."
  },
