    "chunk_size_bytes": 1691,
    "chunk_text": "This year marks the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, as well as the 90th anniversary of the victory of the Long March, and the opening year of the 15th Five-Year Plan. Looking back on China's remarkable achievements, the most fundamental guarantee is the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China. Entering the new era, under the guidance of President Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military,\u00a0 the PLA upgrades military equipment, optimizes troop structure and enhances overall combat capabilities to safeguard national security and global peace.\n\nThe Chinese military has actively participated in UN peacekeeping operations, international counter-terrorism cooperation, and counter-piracy escort missions, providing an increasing amount of international public goods and demonstrating the responsibility and commitment as a major country. The stronger China grows, the more peaceful the world becomes; the more China develops, the more prosperous the world gets.\n\nThe military-to-military relations between China and Sri Lanka are battle-tested. In recent years, military cooperation has been further deepened in multiple fields, covering defense consultations, personnel training, equipment and technical exchanges, etc. In the aftermath of Cyclone Ditwah, China provided the Sri Lankan Ministry of Defence with supplies valued at 10 million RMB. As always, China stands ready to work with Sri Lanka to build strategic trust and continue to firmly support each other.\n\nBuilding on past achievements, we will strive for even greater success. My colleagues and I will continue to make greater contributions to China-Sri Lanka friendship."
