    "language": "en",
    "md5": "37e4fd558ca5cdb6f1993cf4b0f7367c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1887,
    "chunk_text": "LOLC Finance expands islandwide reach\n\nLOLC Finance Chief Operating Officer Montini Warnakula and Head of Channels Prasanna Karandagolla at ribbon-cutting ceremony marking LOLC Finance Mirigama branch opening\n\nLOLC Finance Head of Gold Loan Nishantha Jayasekara and Head of SME and Personal Finance Charith Jagoda at ribbon-cutting ceremony marking LOLC Finance Galagedara branch opening\n\nReinforcing its commitment to bringing trusted financial services closer to communities across Sri Lanka, LOLC Finance PLC, the country\u2019s largest non-bank financial institution (NBFI), has further expanded its islandwide footprint through the opening of two new branches in Mirigama and Galagedara.\n\nThe Mirigama branch, located at No. 14/1, Amarathunga Mawatha, Mirigama, was ceremonially declared open on June 18, 2026, while the Galagedara branch, situated at No. 179/B, Rambukkana Road, Galagedara, commenced operations on July 02, 2026.\n\nThe openings mark another significant milestone in LOLC Finance\u2019s ongoing strategy of enhancing accessibility and delivering convenient financial solutions to the customers across the country.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s largest NBFI, LOLC Finance continues to strengthen its presence in key regional markets, ensuring that individuals, entrepreneurs and businesses have greater access to a comprehensive portfolio of financial products and services.\n\nThe new branches have been established to meet the growing demand for reliable financial solutions while supporting the economic aspirations of the communities they serve.\n\nThe Mirigama and Galagedara branches will offer the full spectrum of LOLC Finance\u2019s services, including savings and fixed deposits, leasing facilities, business and personal loans, gold loans, SME financing, digital financial solutions and a range of value-added financial services designed to cater to the diverse needs of customers."
  },
