    "chunk_size_bytes": 762,
    "chunk_text": "The Police stressed that no government institution or private organisation will ever request OTPs, CVV numbers, bank passwords or other confidential banking details over the telephone or through social media.\n\nThe public has been advised not to click on suspicious web links, download files from unknown sources or scan unverified QR codes. Anyone who receives forged documents bearing government logos has been urged to report the matter to the nearest police station immediately.\n\nPolice further reminded the public that no fees are charged for criminal investigations. Victims or anyone targeted by such scams can contact the Computer Crime Investigation Division on 011-2300756 or 071-8592918 and 071-8591765, or visit the CID in person to lodge a complaint."
