    "md5": "87541480e5c176d6e81f386436fccef4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1743,
    "chunk_text": "Regenerate: The ESG Strategy Shaping the Future of Hayleys Plantations\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s plantation sector is being reshaped by climate change, biodiversity loss, evolving regulations and rising expectations for responsible business. In response, Hayleys Plantations has launched Regenerate\u00a0 a unified ESG Roadmap that brings together, Kelani Valley Plantations PLC, Talawakelle Tea Estates PLC and Horana Plantations PLC under one measurable transformation agenda. The strategy is built around a clear ambition to reduce environmental impact, restore natural systems, strengthen plantation communities and future-proof market access.\n\n\u201cRegenerate marks a significant evolution in our sustainability journey. Our ambition extends beyond reducing impact to restoring ecosystems, empowering communities and strengthening long-term business resilience. By bringing together the strengths of our three plantation companies, we are creating measurable value for people, nature and the economy.\u201d Dr. Roshan Rajadurai, Managing Director, Hayleys Plantations.\n\nThe scale of the transformation is significant. Hayleys Plantations contributes approximately 4.6% of Sri Lanka\u2019s tea production and 3.9% of national rubber production, while supporting more than 15,000 employees and nearly 140,000 members of plantation communities. Its ESG platform is supported by 40 certifications, 14 management systems and more than 150 national and international awards, reflecting years of investment in responsible plantation management. Building on this scale, Regenerate brings the Sector\u2019s sustainability initiatives under one integrated ESG framework focused on climate action, resource efficiency, biodiversity, community wellbeing and strong governance."
  },
