    "chunk_size_bytes": 1346,
    "chunk_text": "The scale of the transformation is significant. Hayleys Plantations contributes approximately 4.6% of Sri Lanka\u2019s tea production and 3.9% of national rubber production, while supporting more than 15,000 employees and nearly 140,000 members of plantation communities. Its ESG platform is supported by 40 certifications, 14 management systems and more than 150 national and international awards, reflecting years of investment in responsible plantation management. Building on this scale, Regenerate brings the Sector\u2019s sustainability initiatives under one integrated ESG framework focused on climate action, resource efficiency, biodiversity, community wellbeing and strong governance.\n\nRegenerative agriculture lies at the heart of the Roadmap. Hayleys Plantations aims to expand regenerative agricultural practices to 90% of cultivated land and introduce precision technologies across 75% of estates. GIS mapping, drones, digital field records and AI-supported decision-making are expected to improve crop management, water use, nutrient efficiency and climate resilience. At the same time, the Sector has committed to zero conversion of natural forests and the expansion of biodiversity restoration across estate landscapes\n\nWhile the three plantation companies operate under one Roadmap, each contributes a distinct area of ESG leadership."
