    "md5": "5f608df14d272995f9cf1bcf29ff5493",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1975,
    "chunk_text": "The Global ESG & Sustainability Conference and Awards is one of the region\u2019s premier sustainability platforms, bringing together leading organizations, policymakers, sustainability experts, and innovators from across the Asia-Pacific region. The awards celebrate organizations that are setting new benchmarks in Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) excellence and climate leadership through independently evaluated performance and measurable impact.\n\nRepresenting Hayleys Fabric PLC at the awards ceremony, Mr. Lakmal Diyawaththege proudly accepted the Climate Action Award on behalf of the company. His participation symbolized the collective efforts of the entire Hayleys Fabric team in advancing the organization\u2019s sustainability vision and delivering meaningful climate action.\n\nThis recognition belongs to every member of the Hayleys Fabric family. Winning this award on a global stage is a testament to our shared commitment to embedding sustainability into every aspect of our business. It reflects years of dedication, innovation, and collaboration in building a low-carbon, resilient, and responsible manufacturing business.\n\nHayleys Fabric\u2019s climate action journey is driven by a series of focused sustainability initiatives. These include its Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi)-validated Net Zero targets, investments in renewable energy, decarbonization programmes, circular manufacturing innovations, water stewardship efforts, and strong ESG governance. Through its GreenCatalyst, ESG Roadmap 2030, the company continues to align business growth with environmental responsibility and measurable climate impact.\n\nReceiving the Climate Action Award further strengthens Hayleys Fabric PLC\u2019s position as one of South Asia\u2019s leading sustainable textile manufacturers and reinforces its commitment to accelerating decarbonization, responsible manufacturing, and long-term value creation for customers, communities, employees, and the environment."
