    "chunk_size_bytes": 1181,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s transition towards a greener economy will require long-term commitment, strategic investment, and collective action across both the public and private sectors.\n\nGovernment policy, financial innovation, corporate leadership, and responsible consumer behaviour must work together to create an ecosystem that rewards sustainability.\n\nGreen finance is not merely about funding environmentally friendly projects\u2014it represents a fundamental transformation in how capital is allocated, risks are managed, and value is created. For Sri Lanka, it offers an opportunity to build an economy that is resilient, inclusive, resource-efficient, and globally competitive.\n\nThe future of sustainable investment is no longer a distant vision. It is already shaping financial markets around the world. By embracing green finance today, Sri Lanka can unlock new investment opportunities, support climate action, strengthen economic growth, and create lasting value for future generations. Businesses, investors, policymakers, and financial institutions all have an important role to play in ensuring that sustainable finance becomes a cornerstone of the nation\u2019s development journey."
