    "chunk_size_bytes": 1768,
    "chunk_text": "Shared access to vehicles, equipment, office space, and digital platforms reduces unnecessary consumption while improving resource utilisation.\n\nThese business models create recurring revenue while reducing environmental impacts.\n\nGreen loans, sustainability-linked financing, and ESG investment funds increasingly support projects involving:\n\nInvestors are increasingly recognising that circular economy businesses often demonstrate greater resilience, lower operational risks, and stronger long-term value creation.\n\nSuccessful implementation of circular economy principles requires supportive public policy.\n\nPublic-private partnerships will be essential for scaling circular economy initiatives across industries.\n\nEducation and public awareness campaigns also play an important role in encouraging responsible consumption and waste reduction.\n\nConsumers increasingly influence corporate sustainability strategies through their purchasing decisions.\n\nGrowing demand for environmentally responsible products encourages businesses to reduce packaging, improve recyclability, minimise waste, and disclose sustainability performance.\n\nSimple consumer actions such as repairing products, recycling household waste, reducing single-use plastics, and supporting sustainable brands contribute significantly to building a circular economy. Businesses that understand changing consumer expectations are better positioned to strengthen customer loyalty and market competitiveness.\n\nThe transition towards a circular economy represents one of the most significant economic opportunities of the coming decades. Rather than viewing environmental sustainability as a cost, businesses are increasingly recognising it as a catalyst for innovation, efficiency, and long-term growth."
