    "md5": "cb19d86ca1a4d583fb3ea02a6a8f5e83",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "A: Reaching the 300-library milestone represents far more than a numerical achievement. It reflects over a decade of consistent investment in Sri Lanka\u2019s future through education. Since opening the very first \u2018Pahasara\u2019 library on 1 March 2013, our objective has remained unchanged, to empower children by improving access to quality learning environments and creating opportunities that extend well beyond the classroom.\n\nToday, as we move steadily towards establishing our 300th library, we are proud to see how the initiative has become an integral part of Seylan Bank\u2019s broader commitment to creating meaningful and lasting social impact across Sri Lanka.\n\nQ: What inspired the creation of the \u2018Pahasara\u2019 initiative in the first place?\n\nA: Our inspiration came from a simple belief that every child deserves access to quality educational resources regardless of where they live. We recognised that where a child is born should never determine the opportunities available to learn, grow, and realise their potential. Through Seylan Tikiri, we had already spent many years encouraging children to develop healthy financial habits. Naturally, we began exploring how we could further support children\u2019s overall development in a way that would generate lasting benefits for both individuals and communities.\n\nLibraries became the ideal platform because they are gateways to opportunity, imagination, and lifelong learning, not simply places that house books. They are spaces where curiosity is nurtured, confidence grows, and young minds begin to discover their potential. We wanted to combine the habit of reading with the habit of saving and creating a meaningful connection between knowledge and responsibility."
  },
