    "chunk_id": "2026-07-23-dailyftlk-62b48ee0-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5d0a02ff1a49009bacef1be17a63d518",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1946,
    "chunk_text": "Hemas Embeds Sustainability  at the Core of its Business\n\nAt Hemas, environmental, social and governance thinking is not a checklist sitting alongside strategy. It is treated as part of how the Group grows, manages risk and creates value\n\nBy the end of FY2025/26, Hemas Holdings PLC had helped collect 2.9 million kilograms of plastic from the environment, a large amount of waste that would otherwise have ended up in landfills or waterways. This is not a statistic for an annual report. It is a marker of how Hemas has moved sustainability from the margins of the business to the center of it.\n\nAt Hemas, environmental, social and governance thinking is not a checklist sitting alongside strategy. It is treated as part of how the Group grows, manages risk and creates value.\n\nSustainability is also anchored in Hemas\u2019 purpose of enriching lives.\u00a0 This purpose is the lens through which the Group makes decisions - not just about what it does for communities, but about how it runs its businesses day to day.\n\nClimate change, resource scarcity and shifting consumer expectations are reshaping every industry. Hemas chose to treat these as strategic questions, not just compliance ones. That thinking produced the Group\u2019s Environmental Agenda 2030, built around two priorities: responsible plastic consumption and efficient use of natural resources.\n\nThe most visible commitment under this agenda is plastic neutrality by 2030 - recovering as much plastic as it puts into the market. The 2.9 million kilograms collected so far is real progress toward a circular economy. Alongside this, Hemas is improving water efficiency and expanding renewable energy use across its operations, building resilience into the business itself.\n\nSustainability at Hemas is not confined to environmental metrics. It shows up in how the Group thinks about social impact - not as scattered good deeds, but as an extension of what its businesses already do well."
  },
