    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ca024277c6e0da51c3e867884d3544c4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1887,
    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka: Pioneering the Nation\u2019s Sustainable Future\n\nSri Lanka is entering a defining phase in its sustainability journey, as ESG considerations move from the margins of corporate reporting to the centre of business strategy and public-sector accountability.\n\nFor the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka), this is a natural extension of a role it has fulfilled for decades: strengthening trust, transparency and accountability. As the sole standard-setter, the Institute plays a critical role in aligning the country with global sustainability reporting developments through the adoption and localisation of the International Sustainability Standards Board\u2019s (ISSB) IFRS S1 and S2 standards as SLFRS S1 and S2. In doing so, it provides Sri Lankan organisations with a robust, internationally aligned framework for disclosing sustainability-related risks and opportunities.\n\nHowever, effective sustainability action requires more than standards alone. Recognising this, CA Sri Lanka is committed to building the capabilities, governance frameworks and professional expertise needed to translate sustainability requirements into meaningful action. Through professional development, thought leadership, standard-setting and stakeholder engagement, the Institute is helping organisations embed sustainability into governance, strategy, risk management and decision-making, while elevating the quality, consistency and credibility of sustainability disclosures.\n\nImportantly, this commitment extends beyond corporate reporting. Through initiatives supporting stronger sustainability governance and the development of sustainability reporting in the public sector, the accountancy profession is responding to the sustainability agenda across the wider economy and contributing to the global pursuit of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
