    "chunk_index": 3,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "88f865762667059b87c1dfd3e194005d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "The introduction of SRS 1 represents an important step towards enhancing transparency and accountability in public-sector sustainability reporting. It will support public-sector entities in communicating information on sustainability-related matters and the impacts of their activities, helping stakeholders better understand how public resources and national development efforts intersect with broader sustainability objectives.\n\nStandards and frameworks, however, are only part of the equation. Their effective implementation requires professionals with the knowledge and skills to translate global requirements into meaningful business action.\n\nTo address this need, CA Sri Lanka has introduced the Certified Sustainability Reporting & Strategy Advisor (CSRSA) qualification through its Faculty of Sustainability Reporting & ESG Leadership.\n\nThe professional qualification is structured as a progressive three-tier pathway:\n\nLevel 1 \u2013 Foundation: Advanced Certificate in Sustainability Reporting & Strategy, establishing a strong foundation in sustainability concepts, frameworks and reporting.\n\nLevel 2 \u2013 Application: Diploma in Sustainability Reporting & Strategy, focusing on applying sustainability frameworks, integrating reporting requirements into business strategy and developing effective disclosures.\n\nLevel 3 \u2013 Expert: Higher Diploma in Sustainability Reporting & Strategy, providing advanced expertise in areas including sustainability assurance, climate transition pathways and global regulatory alignment.\n\nThe CSRSA pathway is designed to develop professionals who can help organisations understand sustainability standards, identify relevant risks and opportunities, develop meaningful metrics and greenhouse gas reduction pathways, and integrate sustainability into governance, risk management and long-term strategy."
  },
  {
