    "md5": "0794939ee93aadf2c1de537f2d633900",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1953,
    "chunk_text": "The initiative includes the reintroduction of native plant species, improvement of soil health, increased water infiltration and retention, enhanced biodiversity and the creation of stable habitats for flora and fauna.\n\nBuilding on its commitment to sustainability and stakeholder engagement, the ESG Pavilion 2026 provides a platform for education, dialogue and collaboration. The month-long campaign brings together employees, business leaders and external stakeholders through educational sessions, practical activities, governance awareness and community outreach to encourage participation and collective action.\n\nThe programme spans environmental conservation, safety, governance and social responsibility. Activities include blue carbon awareness sessions, visits to Advantis\u2019 mangrove restoration sites, the 100 for 100 Road Safety Project, sessions on governance, risk management and ESG disclosures and diversity, equity and inclusion (DE&I) initiatives.\n\nBy extending engagement to schools, suppliers, industry partners and local communities, ESG Pavilion 2026 encourages knowledge sharing and collective action. Leadership participation reinforces accountability for advancing HELIOS, while the month-long format allows key priorities to be explored through sustained engagement.\n\nFor Advantis, ESG excellence lies in connecting operational responsibility with purposeful environmental action, empowered people and accountable governance. Through HELIOS, the Group continues to integrate sustainability into the way it operates, making responsible decisions that strengthen the business, support communities and contribute towards a more sustainable future.\n\nAs the transportation and logistics sector continues to evolve, Advantis remains committed to creating value beyond the services it delivers by building resilience, fostering collaboration and driving positive impact for its stakeholders and the environments in which it operates."
