    "chunk_size_bytes": 1726,
    "chunk_text": "SAGT stands as a cornerstone of the Port of Colombo, consistently proving that operational excellence and responsible practices are inseparable. As the only terminal in the Port of Colombo to consistently publish an independently accredited sustainability report aligned with global standards, SAGT has reinforced its commitment to transparency and long-term value creation.\n\nSAGT is accelerating this path through strategic investments, including the purchase of two electric forklifts and an electric vehicle for safety inspections in FY 2025/26 and plans to introduce 30 electric prime mover trucks to reduce Scope 1 emissions. Furthermore, the investment in four new twin-lift STS cranes, increasing twin-lift capability from five to nine units, improves operational efficiency while enhancing energy efficiency per container move.\n\nEnvironmental stewardship is further demonstrated through ongoing conservation efforts, such as support for the Benthara River Mangrove Complex and annual beach clean-ups in partnership with MEPA. Furthermore, the terminal consistently implements best practices in water stewardship and utilises a dedicated hazardous cargo leaking bay to prevent environmental contamination.\n\nDriving a significant social milestone, SAGT has increased female representation from 4% to 6.9% over the past two reporting periods by integrating women into operational shift roles, with a target of 10% by 2029. To sustain this momentum, the Company promotes an equal environment by expanding career opportunities for females, implementing industry-first anti-sexual harassment and paternity leave policies, and establishing mentorship programs that empower the next generation of women in the maritime sector."
