    "md5": "a0d3be03bda1945550c25514f6d8e98c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1858,
    "chunk_text": "\u200bCooray also praised the founders, Karen Rubera and Gayan Senanayake, pointing out that their shared background as Chartered Accountants brings a rare combination of precision and courage to the enterprise, resulting in a business built to last.\n\n\u200bSpeaking at the launch event, Invest Lab Managing Director and founder Karen Rubera emphasised the shifting demands of modern enterprises, noting that businesses today are actively seeking simplicity and efficiency in their operations rather than dealing with fragmented service providers.\n\n\u200b\u201cThey don\u2019t want to coordinate with one company for HR, one company for legal, one company for finance, etc. They want one trusted partner, a team that understands their business, one place that they can turn to with confidence. That inspired our next chapter,\u201d Rubera said.\n\n\u200bShe noted that Right Vantage was created with a clear purpose to simplify how businesses access corporate support services by bringing everything together under one roof.\n\n\u200b\u201cBecause when businesses spend less time managing administration, they have more time to focus on innovation, on growth and creating value. This is the advantage we want every client to experience,\u201d she added.\n\nHemas Centre of Excellence Finance Services General Manager Chamila Cooray\n\n\u200bWhile the new company focuses on domestic market expansion, Rubera reaffirmed that the core values of integrity, professionalism, reliability and partnership will continue to guide their operations. The leadership team is also eyeing significant capacity building in the near term to support their widening service portfolio.\n\n\u200b\u201cIn the next 12 to 18 months, we plan to double the number of employees,\u201d Rubera stated, signalling strong confidence in the company\u2019s future growth and the expanding market for integrated corporate solutions in Sri Lanka."
