    "md5": "c6fabea8df7793d8043ba044cc04fc80",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1878,
    "chunk_text": "The Faculty of Brands launches Spot On platform\n\nTo spotlight and learn from best marketing strategies in Sri Lanka\n\nSpot On, presented by The Faculty of Brands (TFOB), made its debut with five brands taking the stage to share the thinking, strategy, challenges and outcomes behind some of the country\u2019s most talked about campaigns and brand strategies.\n\nCreated in line with TFOB\u2019s vision of bridging the gap between local and global marketing expertise, Spot On was built with the intention of learning from each other as one industry.\n\nElephant House Ice Cream, Ritzbury Roccoa, Prima Kottu Mee, Celeste and CBL each delivered a presentation that gave the audience the rare opportunity to engage directly with the minds behind the work.\n\nRecently, Bay 7 at Trace Expert City in Colombo was filled to capacity. Four hundred plus brand builders, students and industry leaders gathered for something that had not quite existed in Sri Lanka before, a platform dedicated entirely to real Sri Lankan brand stories, told by the people who built them.\n\nWhat made the evening particularly significant was not just the content on stage but the philosophy behind the platform itself. The first edition of Spot On was offered entirely free of charge, a deliberate decision by the TFOB team, made possible through the support of sponsors including Watawala Tea, Cycle, Sustagen, HNB Life, Emerging Media, Domino\u2019s, Roza, Sunquick, Elephant House Cream Soda and Imorich.\n\nTFOB Co-Founder and CEO Gayendra Rajapaksha said, \u201cIf our country\u2019s stories and our brands\u2019 stories are crafted the right way, they can play a powerful role in uplifting our economy. As brand builders and storytellers, we have a great responsibility to take our economy forward through the stories we tell. In our common cause, we don\u2019t compete with each other. We compete with the rest of the world.\u201d"
  },
