    "chunk_size_bytes": 1336,
    "chunk_text": "The bill nobody budgets for: Healthcare and the retirement gap in Sri Lanka\n\nMost people, when they think about retirement, think about income. Will there be enough to cover food, utilities, and the basics of daily life? That question is important. But there is a second question that sits right behind it, quieter and far more expensive, and most people do not ask it until it is already upon them. What happens when you get sick?\n\nHealthcare in retirement is not an occasional inconvenience. For most Sri Lankans, it becomes one of the largest and most unpredictable expenses of the post-work years. It arrives gradually at first, and then all at once. A routine check-up becomes a specialist referral. A specialist referral leads to investigations. Investigations lead to a diagnosis. A diagnosis leads to medication that never stops. And running alongside all of it, quietly compounding, is an inflation rate for healthcare that outpaces most other costs a retiree faces.\n\nThis is the retirement expense that most financial plans either underestimate or ignore entirely. It is a gap that Ceylinco Life, Sri Lanka\u2019s life insurance market leader for 22 consecutive years, has observed widen steadily across the communities it serves and the thousands of policyholders whose retirement journeys it has accompanied over three decades."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-23-islandlk-02c4b591",
    "num": "islandlk-02c4b591",
    "date_str": "2026-07-23",
    "description": "The bill nobody budgets for: Healthcare and the retirement gap in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/the-bill-nobody-budgets-for-healthcare-and-the-retirement-gap-in-sri-lanka/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
