    "chunk_text": "The two sides appear to be preparing for a forever war. Iran\u2019s preparations began as far back as 2003, when it felt the need to reinforce its defenses to avoid becoming another Iraq under the mighty US military. To conquer Iraq, the US-led coalition took only weeks. After heavy aerial bombing decimated Iraq\u2019s military assets, the ground invasion began with the help of the Kurds in the north and the tacit support of the Shiites in the south, for Saddam Hussein\u2019s tyrannical rule had antagonised the two main ethnic groups, which together formed 80 per cent of the population.\n\nMuch of the state\u2019s revenue has gone into bolstering the country\u2019s defence in anticipation of US aggression, even though it is economically painful.\n\nIran has still not exhausted its missile and drone arsenal, despite daily use. Its attacks have become more precise, with missiles destroying US military radars and posing a serious threat to more than 50,000 US troops stationed across the Gulf region.\n\nEqually devastating is Iran\u2019s weaponisation of the Strait of Hormuz. It accuses the US of failing to honour the Memorandum of Understanding signed on June 17/18, particularly Clause 5, which Iran claims explicitly grants it control over the strait. Ships that do not obey Iran\u2019s directives are attacked, prompting US President Donald Trump to warn on Wednesday that for every Iranian strike on a ship in the Strait of Hormuz, the US will destroy a vital bridge or power station in Iran."
