    "chunk_size_bytes": 688,
    "chunk_text": "Supermarket fined Rs. 500,000 for selling Nadu rice above controlled price\n\nColombo, July 24 (Daily Mirror) - A supermarket in Gampola has been fined Rs. 500,000 after pleading guilty to selling locally produced Nadu rice above the government-controlled maximum retail price.\n\nAccording to the Consumer Affairs Authority (CAA), the supermarket was found selling Nadu rice at Rs. 240 per kilogram, exceeding the prescribed maximum retail price of Rs. 230 per kilogram, during a raid conducted by CAA officers on June 23.\n\nWhen the case was taken up before the Gampola Magistrate\u2019s Court, the supermarket admitted to the offence, and the court imposed a fine of Rs. 500,000, the CAA said."
  },
