    "chunk_size_bytes": 1820,
    "chunk_text": "My wife and I have also had the privilege of meeting many sincere friends from Sri Lanka\u2019s Government, Parliament, political parties, media, think tanks, Buddhist community, civil society, and youth groups. Together, we have written a new chapter in carrying forward the traditional friendship between China and Sri Lanka and created countless beautiful memories.\n\nOur two countries are jointly advancing the building of a community with a shared future for humanity and implementing the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative, the Global Civilisation Initiative, and the Global Governance Initiative so as to address global challenges and create a brighter future for the world. The China-Sri Lanka friendship reflects the shared aspirations of our peoples, and China-Sri Lanka cooperation represents the trend of the times\n\nToday, they continue to flourish and shine with renewed vitality in the new era. The friendly relations between China and Sri Lanka are rooted in deep historical ties, a solid political foundation, strong bonds of shared interests, and broad social support.\n\nOver the past six years, we have together weathered the test of the COVID-19 pandemic, joined hands to tide over Sri Lanka\u2019s economic difficulties, rallied to withstand the impact of Cyclone Ditwah, and stood shoulder to shoulder in coping with the energy crisis triggered by the Middle East conflict.\n\nNo matter how the political landscape changes or how the international situation evolves, China and Sri Lanka have always stood firmly together, carrying forward the spirit of independence, self-reliance, solidarity, and mutual assistance enshrined in the Rubber-Rice Pact. Together, we share weal and woe and set a fine example of friendly coexistence and mutually beneficial cooperation among countries."
  },
