    "chunk_size_bytes": 1171,
    "chunk_text": "He said exporters must also prepare for the EU Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR), which begins applying from August 12, 2026, and the EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR), whose due diligence obligations take effect for larger companies on December 30, 2026.\n\nAssistant Manager \u2013 Business Communications and Marketing at Peterson Solutions Sri Lanka, Dulini Wijeratne, said businesses should view compliance as a strategic investment rather than an additional cost.\n\n\u201cThe question regulators, investors and consumers are increasingly asking is no longer whether a company has sustainability ambitions. The question is: Can you prove it?\u201d she said.\n\nPeterson Solutions Sri Lanka will conduct a complimentary webinar titled \u201cESG Reporting Basics: Why, When & How\u201d on July 29 to help businesses understand and prepare for the evolving regulatory requirements.\n\nSri Lanka secures 10% US tariff rate: JAAF thanks the President and government for decisive action\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
