    "chunk_size_bytes": 1840,
    "chunk_text": "Over these 2,000 days, the bustling streets of Colombo, the serene and sacred Cultural Triangle, the misty and lush tea plantations of the up-country, the historic Galle Fort where the East meets the West, the ancient sites echoing with millennia-old heroic legacies, the distinctive local cuisine, and the culturally vibrant festivities\u2014all have shown us this land\u2019s exceptional natural endowments, splendid civilization, and magnificent history. My wife and I have also had the privilege of meeting many sincere friends from Sri Lanka\u2019s government, parliament, political parties, media, think tanks, Buddhist community, civil society, and youth groups. Together, we have written a new chapter in carrying forward the traditional friendship between China and Sri Lanka and created countless beautiful memories.\n\nIn 2025, President Xi Jinping and other Chinese leaders met with President Dissanayake and Prime Minister Amarasuriya during their visits to China, reaching important consensus and fruitful outcomes of cooperation. These interactions have provided new strategic guidance for the development of bilateral relations. Today, political mutual trust between our two countries has continued to consolidate, economic and trade cooperation has further expanded, people-to-people and cultural exchanges have grown increasingly rich, and interactions at all levels\u2014across departments, regions, and sectors\u2014have become ever closer. At present, China-Sri Lanka relations are facing a historic opportunity to build on past achievements and forge ahead into the future. Both sides are committed to deepening the China-Sri Lanka strategic cooperative partnership featuring sincere mutual assistance and everlasting friendship, painting a splendid picture of a China-Sri Lanka community with a shared future through concrete actions."
