    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, Deputy Minister Hennayake highlighted the role young people can play in supporting lifesaving efforts, proposing structured training programmes to develop a volunteer network capable of assisting professional rescue services.\n\nThe meeting was attended by the Chiefs of Staff of the Sri Lanka Army, Navy and Air Force, the Director General of the Sri Lanka Coast Guard, senior officials from the Ministries of Defence, Health, Education, Sports and Youth Affairs, and Tourism, as well as representatives from the Disaster Management Centre, Sri Lanka Police, the Institute of National Security Studies, the Civil Security Department, and the Sri Lanka Life Saving Association."
