    "chunk_size_bytes": 1453,
    "chunk_text": "On Sunday, the Iranian foreign ministry said that technical and political consultations between the two sides were ongoing via Omani intermediaries. Talks over the strait were, Iran said, productive.\n\nThe Pentagon rushed more forces, weaponry and supplies to the Middle East in recent days to prepare for any escalation.\n\nSince the campaign began, the US has damaged or destroyed an increasing number of railway bridges that civilians use but that also enable Iranian commanders to send supplies to the southern coastal region near the strait.\n\nOfficials told the NYT that increased attacks on those kinds of targets, as well as energy facilities and Iran\u2019s nuclear sites, including Pickaxe Mountain, were still under consideration.\n\nUS officials stress that military options remain on the table should negotiations fail or were Iran to launch further attacks. However, it represents the clearest indication yet that the White House is searching for an off-ramp after five months of conflict.\n\nThere is also growing unease within Mr Trump\u2019s inner circle over the prospect of being drawn into a prolonged regional conflict which has triggered backlash domestically.\n\nCNN reported that close advisers had voiced concerns over both the strategic and political costs of expanding the war, particularly given the strain on US military resources, the loss of lives and uncertainty over whether further strikes would fundamentally alter Iran\u2019s behaviour."
