    "md5": "9cb1a523651fb43e04096b301fd6e124",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1566,
    "chunk_text": "Pelwatte breaks ground for liquid milk facility in Kurunegala\n\nChairman Ariyaseela Wickremanayake and Managing Director Akmal Wickramanayake perform the ceremonial groundbreaking\n\nPelwatte Dairy Industries has officially broken ground on its Greenfield Liquid Milk Manufacturing Facility in Kurunegala.\n\nSet to open in July 2027, the facility represents Pelwatte\u2019s transition from its longstanding leadership in full cream milk powder into liquid dairy products, strengthening access to fresh, locally manufactured dairy products for Sri Lankan consumers.\n\nCommenting on the milestone, Managing Director Akmal Wickramanayake said, \u201cBy bringing world-class liquid milk production to Sri Lanka and producing products that promote healthier families while strengthening the country\u2019s dairy industry, this facility enables us to build on that legacy. When the facility begins operations in 2027, we look forward to welcoming consumers to a new chapter of Pelwatte.\u201d\n\nChairman Ariyaseela Wickremanayake added, \u201cOur long-term goals of developing the country\u2019s dairy industry, creating lasting value for local communities and farmers, and guaranteeing that future generations have access to nutritious, locally produced dairy products are all reflected in this project.\u201d\u00a0 \u00a0Designed to support future growth in Sri Lanka\u2019s dairy sector while meeting international quality and food safety standards, the Greenfield Liquid Milk Manufacturing Facility symbolizes the next stage in Pelwatte\u2019s journey towards becoming a comprehensive dairy nutrition company."
  },
