    "chunk_text": "British Council Sri Lanka transfers vocational qualification attestation to TVEC\n\nChange takes effect in compliance with Sri Lankan law, ensuring smooth transitions\n\nFrom August 1, 2026, students and graduates requiring attestation of vocational or technical qualifications should contact TVEC directly\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka will continue to provide attestation for UK university degrees and graduate diplomas awarded directly by UK awarding bodies\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka and the Tertiary and Vocational Education Commission (TVEC) yesterday announced that the attestation of vocational and technical qualifications will transfer from British Council Sri Lanka to the TVEC, with effect from August 1, 2026.\n\nFrom August 1, 2026, the attestation of vocational or technical qualifications \u2014 including those linked to the UK awarding bodies \u2014 will be done by the TVEC. British Council Sri Lanka will continue to process all applications submitted on or before July 31, 2026.\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka will continue to provide attestation for the UK university degrees, graduate diplomas awarded directly by the UK awarding bodies, Cambridge International, Pearson Edexcel and OxfordAQA O Level and A Level certificates as well as IELTS and Aptis certificates and ACCA qualifications.\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka and TVEC have also worked with the UK\u2019s Department for Business and Trade to ensure the UK awarding bodies understand Sri Lanka\u2019s regulatory requirements.\n\nThe UK qualifications remain recognised and valued in Sri Lanka \u2013 the transition ensures that the attestation is carried out in full compliance with Tertiary and Vocational Education (TVE) Act No. 20 of 1990, which establishes the TVEC as the national statutory authority responsible for the regulation, coordination and quality assurance of tertiary and vocational education in Sri Lanka."
  },
