    "md5": "be4827cf17e904d35450d91eb38a11f5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1852,
    "chunk_text": "The UK qualifications remain recognised and valued in Sri Lanka \u2013 the transition ensures that the attestation is carried out in full compliance with Tertiary and Vocational Education (TVE) Act No. 20 of 1990, which establishes the TVEC as the national statutory authority responsible for the regulation, coordination and quality assurance of tertiary and vocational education in Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cBritish Council Sri Lanka is committed to operating fully within the Sri Lankan law and to supporting the integrity of the country\u2019s education system. Our close collaboration with the TVEC over the past year has ensured that this transition is smooth, transparent and protects the interests of the students and graduates.\n\nWe are confident that the UK qualifications will continue to be recognised and valued and that this change strengthens the reliability of attestation services in Sri Lanka,\u201d said British Council Sri Lanka Country Director Orlando Edwards.\n\n\u201cThe TVEC is the sole government body in Sri Lanka authorised to recognise the vocational and technical qualifications in all fields of learning, from certificate level up to higher diploma level. This is a practical change that provides greater clarity for the students and providers while ensuring that vocational qualification attestation is carried out by the statutory authority responsible under the Sri Lankan law.\n\nThe TVEC is well-placed to respond to all requests for attestation in an efficient manner and will take care of the best interests of the Sri Lankan students in attesting qualifications,\u201d said TVEC Director General Dr. K.A. Lalithadheera.\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka has operated a qualification attestation service for many years, providing certified confirmation of qualifications to support students, graduates and professionals seeking opportunities overseas."
