    "chunk_size_bytes": 940,
    "chunk_text": "Sectoral credit data indicates that lending to financial services, consumer finance, and pawning has grown at rates well above the banking system average. Rather than matching loan growth with deposit mobilisation, many licensed finance companies have increasingly turned to commercial bank borrowings to fund their portfolios, according to him.\n\nDespite private sector credit surging by 27.8 percent, overall domestic credit growth remained anchored at 11.1 percent in May 2026. This macro-level stability was enabled by strict government fiscal discipline, which generated large primary surpluses, as well as cost-reflective pricing at state-owned enterprises that curtailed public sector borrowing requirements.\n\nVehicle imports accounted for 9.7 percent\u00a0 of total current account outflows in May 2026, keeping the sector under close regulatory observation as dealer pre-registrations hide its footprint from official registration data."
