    "md5": "e6f0848930595b95a8b56127e2ee7f53",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1412,
    "chunk_text": "Nalin as a novel navigator: Reflections in retrospect\n\nThree months have passed by since the surprise demise of\u00a0 Senior Professor Nalin Abeysekara, Former Dean of the Faculty of Management, Open University of Sri Lanka. It is sad to see good people die young. It happened to my precious son 10 years ago. This time it is with one of my best friends. He is one of the most down to earth scholars that I have ever seen who was high in stature yet humble and humane. This brief reflection is my revered tribute to a remarkable human being on his third month\u203as remembrance.\n\nHe connected Hinniappuhami with Kotler. With his bi-lingual mastery, translating marketing concepts into Sinhala for the benefit of many local entrepreneurs was exemplary. Being a Marketing graduate of University of Sri Jayewardenepura , he was a\u00a0 \u00a0Chartered Marketer and a member of the Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (SLIM) as well. He has contributed many articles to many local and international journals whilst being a popular personality in print media, electronic media as well as social media.\n\nHe obtained his PhD (Marketing and Leadership) and MBA both from the University of Colombo, Sri Lanka. In 2018, he was recognised as an \u201cOutstanding Asian Educator\" by International Association of Scholarly Publishers, Editors and Reviewers (IASPER). I still remember being one of the examiners for his professorship assessment ."
  },
