    "chunk_text": "President discusses issues in developing cricket in Sri Lanka\n\nColombo, July 27 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake held a meeting with the Sri Lanka Cricket (SLC)\n\nTransformation Committee where he discussed the issues and challenges faced in developing cricket in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe meeting was held at the Presidential Secretariat this afternoon, the President\u2019s Media Division (PMD) said.\n\nThe President also considered the support and contribution that could be provided by the Government towards the continued progress and advancement of cricket in the country.\n\nMinister of Youth Affairs and Sports Sunil Kumara Gamage, Chief of Staff to the President Prabath Chandrakeerthi, Chairman of the Sri Lanka Cricket Transformation Committee Eran Wickramaratne and committee members Roshan Mahanama, Avanthi Colombage, Upul Kumarapperuma, Thushira\u00a0Radella, Sidath Wettimuny and Dinal Philip also participated in the meeting."
  },
