    "chunk_text": "Then, Prof. Charitha Herath as the Chairman of the COPE in 2022 suggested during proceedings of his committee to take up the follow-up issue in Parliament and create a mechanism for action against the culprits. In October 2023, COPF Chairman Dr. Harsha De Silva told Parliament that having a representative from the Attorney General\u2019s Department present during meetings of the PAC and COPE would facilitate the utilisation of evidence uncovered during such meetings in future court proceedings.\n\nYet, nothing happened, corruption continued unbated and revelations of frauds during these committee meetings too,\u00a0 continued to be media shows. No government in the past was interested in formulating a mechanism to bring the culprits of corruption to the book. We continue with our pressure on the government to strengthen the mechanisms against corruption, frauds and waste of public funds.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
