    "md5": "b4a0b01139eeb845ce5c99316c586ed8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1667,
    "chunk_text": "France evacuates 4,000 as Gironde wildfire faces renewed heat threat\n\nINDIA TODAY - French authorities ordered nearly 4,000 people to evacuate tourist sites on the Atlantic coast on Tuesday as returning heat threatened firefighters\u2019 fragile hold on a vast wildfire west of Bordeaux. The new evacuations added to a wildfire crisis across south-western Europe, where fires in France and Spain have forced about 330,000 people to leave their homes and holiday accommodation.\n\nIn France, officials said the Gironde fire had been stabilised but not fixed, meaning it could spread again as temperatures rise and humidity falls. In neighbouring Landes, thousands of evacuees were allowed to return after a separate wildfire was brought under control. In Spain, firefighters continued battling several major fires as the country entered its fourth heatwave of the summer.\n\nFirefighters held the Gironde blaze in check through a calm night, controlling flare-ups near coastal dunes and keeping the burned area unchanged at 420 square kilometres. The precautionary evacuation order covered campsites, holiday villages, tourist residences and leisure parks around the resort of Lacanau, including Lacanau Ocean and both shores of Lacanau lake, regional authorities said.\n\n\u201cWe are at a point of fragility,\u201d Eric Brocardi, spokesperson for France\u2019s national firefighters federation, told BFMTV on Tuesday. \u201cWe will continue attacking this fire despite the forecast rise in temperatures.\u201d The fire, burning since last week, has at times turned into a self-feeding firestorm as it spread across an area four times the size of Paris and forced 220,000 people to evacuate."
  },
