    "chunk_text": "SriLankan Airlines expands reach with Maldivian interline partnership\n\nSriLankan Airlines has strengthened its regional connectivity through a new interline agreement with Island Aviation Services, operating as Maldivian. This agreement enables SriLankan Airlines passengers to seamlessly access 17 popular domestic destinations across the Maldives.\n\nThe arrangement is designed to enhance travel convenience by allowing passengers to book journeys involving both carriers under a single electronic ticket. This applies to all inbound and outbound travel via Velana International Airport in Mal\u00e9 and Gan International Airport on Gan Island, ensuring a smooth end-to-end travel experience.\n\nBy connecting SriLankan Airlines\u2019 international network with Maldivian\u2019s extensive domestic operations, the agreement significantly improves access to remote and popular island destinations within the Maldives. This is expected to be particularly beneficial for both leisure and business travellers seeking efficient transfers within the archipelago.\n\nSriLankan Airlines continues to maintain three daily frequencies to Velana International Airport in Male and two weekly frequencies to Gan International Airport on Gan Island, ensuring strong connectivity to the Maldives. The airline operates an extensive international network, with these services providing convenient connections to and from its global destinations.\n\nThis initiative also creates new opportunities for travel agents, tour operators, corporate travel planners, and individual passengers, with more streamlined booking options expected to drive increased passenger traffic and boost sales on both the Mal\u00e9 and Gan routes."
  },
