    "md5": "1cb0e1a78ce70f1a955d88ab99890a79",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1935,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Dockyard returns to profit as ship repair earnings surge\n\nColombo Dockyard PLC swung to a profit in the three months through June as stronger ship repair earnings and lower finance costs outweighed a drop in revenue.\n\nThe group posted a net profit of Rs.80.2 million, reversing a Rs.813.4 million loss a year earlier, according to interim financial statements filed with the Colombo Stock Exchange.\n\nRevenue fell 6.8 percent to Rs.5.84 billion, but cost of sales declined 21.8 percent to Rs.4.63 billion. That lifted gross profit to Rs.1.21 billion from Rs.345.4 million and widened the gross profit margin to 20.7 percent from 5.5 percent.\n\nShip repairing was the strongest-performing business during the quarter. Revenue from the segment climbed 48.4 percent to Rs.3.95 billion, while its result at gross profit level more than doubled to Rs.1.46 billion.\n\nThat helped counter continued weakness in shipbuilding, where revenue declined 61.6 percent to Rs.1.05 billion. The segment remained loss-making at gross profit level, though its loss narrowed to Rs.378.8 million from Rs.899.6 million.\n\nHeavy engineering revenue fell 11.7 percent to Rs.703.6 million, while its segment result dropped to Rs.30.4 million from Rs.480.7 million.\n\nThe company also benefited from a 63.8 percent reduction in net finance expenses to Rs.188.2 million. Administrative expenses, however, rose 18.2 percent to Rs.1.03 billion, while other income declined 57.7 percent to Rs.108.5 million.\n\nProfit attributable to owners was Rs.86.3 million, compared with a loss of Rs.808.4 million in the corresponding quarter. Earnings per share were 22 cents, against a restated loss of Rs.3.51.\n\nThe return to profit did not translate into positive operating cash flow. The group used Rs.678.1 million in operating activities, as trade and other receivables increased by Rs.3.43 billion during the quarter. Trade and other payables rose by Rs.2.35 billion."
  },
