    "chunk_size_bytes": 1377,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka needs accelerated investment in advanced forensic drug analysis for network mapping, expanded digital and cyber forensics to clear backlogs, strengthened financial investigation for asset tracing, and data analytics for intelligence fusion across agencies. Officers must be equipped and trained for this more complex environment. Without this technical upgrade, the campaign will remain one step behind adaptive criminal networks.\n\nThe vast majority of police officers serve with dedication under difficult conditions. While firm action against the corrupt minority must continue without fear or favour, generalised public narratives of failure damage morale and risk creating perverse incentives for shortcuts. Officers deserve clear direction, resources, protection when acting professionally, and recognition of their contribution.\n\nNone of these improvements will succeed in isolation. This is not one-way traffic. Public awareness of the true scale of the menace, combined with a clear understanding of shared responsibility, is essential. The people must recognise that they are simultaneously victims of this threat and the primary beneficiaries of success. With that recognition comes responsibility, to report credible intelligence, support rehabilitation and reintegration, protect young people from recruitment, and reject the stigma that hinders recovery."
