    "md5": "ea0134dc6aa490b0c8726428f2053c42",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1707,
    "chunk_text": "Whatever else is said and done, the most effective, efficient and ultimately most beneficial investment is in robust prevention measures-sustained, consistent and powered by proactive intelligence blended with actionable and strategic intelligence.\n\nWhen these proactive efforts are fused with high-quality actionable intelligence for immediate disruptions and strategic intelligence for long-term policy and systemic interventions, prevention becomes genuinely preventive. It allows authorities to target vulnerabilities in supply chains and recruitment points rather than merely reacting to street-level seizures. Prevention is not soft; it is the hardest and most strategic work. It demands the same professional rigour, resources and intelligence support as enforcement operations, and ultimately delivers far greater returns for the nation.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Police remains the prime law enforcement agency in the country today. It has so far done well in curbing the underworld, criminal syndicates, drug cartels and extremism to a significant extent. This does not mean that everything is in place or that all is well. Root causes persist and continue to be exploited by interested political elements from time to time. These root causes must be systematically eliminated, kept under constant check and decisively wrapped up.\n\nThe main concerns in society today centre on the image of the police and the effectiveness of policing. Are our officers ready to run the extra mile? Are they sufficiently motivated to do so? Over and above the motivating factors lie serious demoralising influences that operate almost continuously through uncertainty and unverified information disseminated via social media."
  },
  {
