    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "36e96a9d751897813c9959165882e69c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1458,
    "chunk_text": "The main concerns in society today centre on the image of the police and the effectiveness of policing. Are our officers ready to run the extra mile? Are they sufficiently motivated to do so? Over and above the motivating factors lie serious demoralising influences that operate almost continuously through uncertainty and unverified information disseminated via social media.\n\nAre our policemen ready for change? Yes. They possess their own pride and dignity. What they require is proper guidance, clear assurance and inspiring leadership.\n\nTo address this challenge effectively, the following practical measures are essential:\n\nEstablish a professional, 24/7 official communication unit with verified social media channels to rapidly counter false narratives with facts rather than allowing misinformation to fill the vacuum.\n\nEnforce strict internal discipline with swift, transparent action against officers who leak sensitive documents or operational information, regardless of rank.\n\nCreate a dedicated monitoring and response capability within the police to track harmful trends early and coordinate timely, factual rebuttals.\n\nFormally engage major social media platforms to secure faster removal of damaging content while launching sustained public media literacy campaigns through community and religious platforms.\n\nProvide visible leadership, clear assurance and institutional protection to honest officers, while maintaining firm accountability."
  },
