    "md5": "d8a670172fee6dfe795099c944feb5c4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1586,
    "chunk_text": "US launches dengue response initiative in Sri Lanka\n\nUS-funded partnership brings American military preventive medicine expertise to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s dengue prevention and vector control capabilities\n\nAs Sri Lanka responds to a significant nationwide dengue outbreak, the US Embassy in Sri Lanka has launched a Public Health Pest Control and Vector-Borne Disease Response program in partnership with the Health Ministry Sri Lanka and National Dengue Control Unit to strengthen the country\u203as ability to prevent, detect, and respond to dengue.\n\nOverseas Humanitarian, Disaster, and Civic Aid (OHDACA) program, the initiative brings together experts from U.S. Army Pacific (USARPAC) and the US Army\u2019s 18th Theatre Medical Command with counterparts from the Health Ministry Sri Lanka to share American expertise in preventive medicine, disease surveillance, entomology, and integrated vector management. Conducted in Colombo, the initiative supports Sri Lanka\u2019s nationwide dengue response, complementing mosquito breeding site eradication efforts, public awareness campaigns, and predictive prevention methodology.\n\nCharg\u00e9 d\u2019Affaires a.i. Jayne Howell said: \u201cDengue continues to pose a serious challenge for families and communities across Sri Lanka. Through this partnership, the United States is sharing American expertise in preventive medicine, entomology, disease surveillance, and vector control. This will strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s response to today\u2019s outbreak while building sustainable capabilities that will protect Sri Lankan communities for years to come.\u201d"
  },
